    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **23 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber`, formatted `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'` where YY is the last two digits of the registration year, following the existing \"assigned field\" pattern (`customerCode`, `namesakeCount`) in the create-owner pipeline.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **New function** `AssignMembershipNumber.java` \u2014 a create-owner pipeline step that reads the already-set `customerCode` and `registrationDate` off the built owner (via `@Val Owner`) and stamps `<customerCode>-M<YY>` in place. YY is `registrationDate.getYear() % 100`, zero-padded to two digits.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** in `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `membershipNumber` step (under governance) after `namesakeCount` and before `save`, so it runs once both `customerCode` and `registrationDate` are resolved, and the assigned value is persisted and returned.\n\n3. **Owner model** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` field mapped to a new `membership_number` column, with getter/setter.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `membership_number` to the `owners` table in all four schema variants (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql).\n\n5. **OpenAPI spec** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (which regenerates `OwnerDto`, so the response carries it and the MapStruct mapper populates it automatically).\n\n6. **OwnerMapper** \u2014 ignored `membershipNumber` on the `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` mapping (it's a server-assigned, read-only field, consistent with `customerCode`/`namesakeCount`).\n\nThe new `Cp14Tests` and all pre-existing tests pass.",
